  "id": "behavioral-model",
  "term": "behavioral model",
  "definition": "A behavioral model is a framework used to explain or predict service use by linking it to factors that predispose a person to act, factors that enable access, and perceived or actual need. In this source, Andersen’s behavioral model is used to understand patterns of children's dental service utilization.",
